<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformations Eliminated
  ======================================================
  This Web.Release.config transformation file has been superseded by environment variables
  and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store for all environment-specific configuration.

  PREVIOUSLY: Build-time Web.config transformations baked configuration into build artifacts,
  preventing immutable deployments and making cloud pipeline configuration difficult.

  NOW (Cloud-Native Pattern):
  Configuration is injected at RUNTIME via the following priority chain:
    1. Environment Variables (highest priority)
       - DB_CONNECTION_STRING  : Amazon RDS / RDS Proxy connection string
       - S3_BUCKET_NAME        : Amazon S3 bucket for file uploads
       - AWS_REGION            : AWS region (e.g., us-east-1)
       Set these in: AWS ECS task definition, Elastic Beanstalk environment properties,
                     AWS Lambda environment variables, or EC2 instance user data.

    2. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (runtime-configurable, no rebuild required)
       Parameter paths used by this application:
         /tour-mgmt/DB_CONNECTION_STRING  (SecureString — encrypted at rest)
         /tour-mgmt/S3_BUCKET_NAME
         /tour-mgmt/AWS_REGION
         /tour-mgmt/CSP/Policy
         /tour-mgmt/ScriptManager/CloudFrontCdnPath
       IAM role on the compute resource must have ssm:GetParameter permission.
       Update parameters via AWS Console, CLI, or SDK — no application rebuild required.

    3. Web.config / appsettings.json (local development fallback only)
       The <connectionStrings> and <appSettings> in Web.config serve as local dev defaults.
       These values are NEVER used in cloud environments where env vars or SSM are set.

  RELEASE-SPECIFIC SETTINGS:
  In cloud environments, release/production settings are controlled via environment variables:
    - ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production   (disables debug output, enables production optimizations)
    - compilation debug attribute is NOT needed — controlled by ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT at runtime
  No build-time transformation is needed — the runtime environment variable controls behavior.

  HOW TO SET PARAMETERS IN AWS SSM PARAMETER STORE:
    aws ssm put-parameter \
      --name "/tour-mgmt/DB_CONNECTION_STRING" \
      --value "Server=<rds-endpoint>;Database=tourdb;User Id=<user>;Password=<pwd>;" \
      --type SecureString \
      --overwrite

    aws ssm put-parameter \
      --name "/tour-mgmt/S3_BUCKET_NAME" \
      --value "tour-management-prod-uploads" \
      --type String \
      --overwrite

  This file is retained as documentation only and is NOT applied during cloud builds.
-->

<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No build-time transformations are applied.
    All environment-specific configuration is externalized to:
      - Environment variables (AWS ECS / Elastic Beanstalk / Lambda)
      - AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (/tour-mgmt/* parameter paths)
    See comments above for the full configuration strategy.

    Previously this file contained:
      <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" />
    This is no longer needed because debug mode is controlled at runtime via
    the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT environment variable, not at build time.
  -->
</configuration>
